@7465[end]. They are first convinced that they are in evil...

@LJ 26[end]. I was thus fully convinced...

@DSS 4[end]. To convince even the natural man, if he is willing to be convinced.

@AR 544. To "pasture all nations with a rod of iron" = through truths from the sense of the letter, and at the same time by rational things from natural light, to convince those who are willing to be convinced. @828.

@CL 295. Those things of which the spirit is convinced, are allotted a place above those which, without consulting reason, enter on authority...

@TCR 344. Conviction (a part of the manifestation of the faith of the New Church).

@796[3]. After conviction, (Luther) began to favour the truths of the New Church...

@SE 2455[end]. In order to convince him...

