@10420. To "corrupt themselves" (Exodus 33:7), when said of worship, = to turn themselves away from the Divine.

@TCR 433. These are means of corruption; to draw men to their side.

@SE 2712. Thus the world is now corrupt...

@AE 410[10]. "A corrupt girdle" (Jeremiah 13:7). Explained. @569[20].

@444[12]. "Ye have corrupted the covenant of Levi" (Malachi 2:8) = That the Church with the Israelites had perverted the truths of the Word, and thence the goods of life, and had thus destroyed conjunction with the Lord. @701[9].

@654[68]. (The signification of "corrupt" further illustrated.) @725[11]. @750[5]. @768[19]. @863[16]. @1201.

@768[24]. "Sons that are corrupters" (Isaiah 1:4) = the falsities of those who are in falsity from that evil.

Cortical.; Corticalis. Cortex. @SE 3811.
See <Brain>.

@AC 3677[end]. Such love to wander only in the rind (of knowledge).

@4052. Under <Beginning-Principium>, see this reference.

@8245. They use a head-covering made of bluish bark.

@8379. Their habitations are lined with bluish bark.

@DLW 366[2]. The cortical or glandular substance forms the surface of the cerebrum, also the surface of the corpora striata... and the middle of the cerebellum and spinal marrow.

@373[2]. The receptacles of the will and understanding are plainly to be seen in the cortical substance, as minute glands.

@TCR 78[4]. As the rind and bark clothe the trunks and branches of trees...

@351[3]. The brain consists of two substances, one of which is glandular, and is called the cortical and cineritious substance... This substance is disposed into clusters like grapes on a vine; these clusterings are its series.

@484. Like bark about wood.

@593. Like the inner bark -philyrae- which adheres to the bark of a tree.

@WE 5030. Like the undulatory creeping of the cortical substances in the brain...

@SE 999. In the ureter, where there is, as it were, a cortical substance...

